            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>To Lucius Betutius Furianus, son of Lucius, of tribe Palatina, first spear of the 1st Italic legion, duovir quinquennalis, duovir for the administration of justice, tresvir, curule aedile, pontifex, flamen of the divine Nerva, patron of the colony, most loving father of the college of textile dealers. This place was given by decree of the decurions.</p>
            </div>
